     1	//! Half-open byte spans with checked construction and UTF-8 substring access.
     2	//!
     3	//! [`ByteSpan`] represents `[start, end)` in bytes, independently of any text.
     4	//! Its endpoints always satisfy `start <= end`; empty spans are valid. Text
     5	//! bounds and UTF-8 boundaries are checked only by [`ByteSpan::slice`].
     6	//! [`SpanError`] identifies validation failures without parsing error messages.
     7	//!
     8	//! # Examples
     9	//!
    10	//! ```
    11	//! use byte_span::ByteSpan;
    12	//!
    13	//! let text = "a🦀z";
    14	//! let crab = ByteSpan::new(1, 5)?;
    15	//! assert_eq!(crab.len(), 4);
    16	//! assert_eq!(crab.slice(text)?, "🦀");
    17	//! assert_eq!(crab.intersection(&ByteSpan::new(3, 6)?), Some(ByteSpan::new(3, 5)?));
    18	//! # Ok::<(), Box<dyn std::error::Error>>(())
    19	//! ```
